from jsonb_array_elements('[{"itemId":"4a469326-cbdb-5185-abb8-e47b04c9b668","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-01","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-01","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 4, 5, 6; activities 1, 2, 5, 6, 7; programme T1.K1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-DB-01","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"Reliable fits arranging a dependable alternative when attendance becomes impossible. The inference concerns the handling of responsibility, not attendance itself.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"She makes sure the group can still depend on the promised work."},{"key":"b","text":"Nothing here establishes nervousness with people."},{"key":"c","text":"She remembers the responsibility and makes an alternative plan."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Personality meaning from stated behaviour","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-P01","ENG7-U01-P02","ENG7-U01-P03","ENG7-U01-P04","ENG7-U01-P32","ENG7-U01-P31"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-01","ENG7-U01-MA-01"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-MB-01","ENG7-U01-MC-01"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Recognise dependability in a successful contingency rather than equate reliability with always attending. Prior promise-keeping examples do not supply the complete alternative-action judgment.","completeSolution":"Reliable fits arranging a dependable alternative when attendance becomes impossible. The inference concerns the handling of responsibility, not attendance itself.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this comple