ndependent human review pending"},"source":null}},{"itemId":"20494a22-562a-5b72-ab04-a317bc96ca31","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-21","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-21","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 17, 18; activities 19; programme T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-DB-21","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The clearer notice explains participation and respects individual choice; it replaces the vague fashion label.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The revision resolves the stated confusion."},{"key":"b","text":"The club explicitly did not choose a winning style."},{"key":"c","text":"That was the uncertainty caused by the first wording, not the final rule."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Main idea of READ-A","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R02","ENG7-U01-R04","ENG7-U01-R05","ENG7-U01-R06","ENG7-U01-R09","ENG7-U01-P23","ENG7-U01-P24"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-21","ENG7-U01-MA-21"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-MB-21","ENG7-U01-MC-21"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Connect the initial confusion with the practical revision, rather than treating the first notice as the final rule. The gist requires the whole sequence.","completeSolution":"The clearer notice explains participation and respects individual choice; it replaces the vague fashion label.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-DB-READ-A","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"666623ab-ba5a-5ef1-908c-edccbd629963","title":"Reading source DB-A","locale":"en","text":"A school club planned a clothes-swap afternoon. Its first notice asked people to bring fashionable clothes. Several students were unsure: did their clothes have to be popular that month?\n\nThe club rewrote the notice. It now asked for clean clothes in good condition, with the size written on a card. People could choose according to fit and personal preference. The club did not select one winning style.\n\nStudents who had misunderstood the first notice now knew what they could bring. A clear description of the event was more useful than a vague fashion label.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"48c7dcad-4c3d-5c13-a79e-8b941a39727a","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-22","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-22","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 17, 18; activities 19; programme T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-DB-22","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The revised notice asks for the size on a card.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The revision removes popularity as the criterion."},{"key":"b","text":"The size is the requested card detail."},{"key":"c","text":"There is no winning style."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"prot