of the event was more useful than a vague fashion label.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"306106fb-7445-504d-a45c-480f64279eb3","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-23","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-23","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 16, 20, 21; activities 18, 21, 22; programme T1.K2, T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-DB-23","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The inspiration during her studies came before the sisters started the brand.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"Starting the brand comes later."},{"key":"b","text":"The inspiration belongs to her earlier studies."},{"key":"c","text":"The passage distinguishes the study period from the later start."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Chronology or contrast from READ-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R01","ENG7-U01-R03","ENG7-U01-R07","ENG7-U01-R08"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-23","ENG7-U01-MA-23"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-MB-23","ENG7-U01-MC-23"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Order inspiration and establishment using during and later, without requiring recall of dates from outside the supplied profile.","completeSolution":"The inspiration during her studies came before the sisters started the brand.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-DB-READ-B","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"e2ea2323-9ab3-59c7-ade7-9a125b781075","title":"Reading source DB-B","locale":"en","text":"The Fashion and Design Chamber of Armenia describes Inga Manukyan''s path to LOOM Weaving. During her art studies, Armenian carpet weaving gave her ideas for clothing. Later, with encouragement from her sister, she developed that idea further. The sisters started LOOM Weaving in 2014.\n\nThe profile connects their knitwear with handmade techniques and modern style. It shows one way a traditional craft can inspire clothing made for the present.","sourceReferences":["https://www.fdc.am/designers/5"],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"3965e2fa-2ab5-5a0e-a3dc-7d056f7c3a0f","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-24","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-24","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 16, 20, 21; activities 18, 21, 22; programme T1.K2, T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-DB-24","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The passage identifies Armenian carpet weaving.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"This is the craft named in the passage."},{"key":"b","text":"The passage does not identify metalworking."},{"key":"c","text":"The passage does not identify pottery."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Supported cultural information from READ-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R01","ENG7-U01-R03","ENG7-U01-R07","ENG7-U01-R08"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-24","ENG7-U01-MA-24"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-MB-24","ENG7-U01-MC-24"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Retrieve the particular craft in this profile; the general fact that a designer draws on Armenian culture is insufficient to choose among these crafts.","completeSolution":"The passage identifies Armenian carpet weaving.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-DB-READ-B","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"e2ea2323-9ab3-59c7-ade7-9a125b781075","title":"Reading source DB-B","locale":"en","text":"The Fashion and Design Chamber of Armenia describes Inga Manukyan''s path to LOOM Weaving. During her art studies, Armenian carpet weaving gave her ideas for clothing. Later, with encouragement from her sister, she developed that idea further. The sisters started LOOM Weaving in 2014.\n\nThe profile connects their knitwear with handmade techniques and modern style. It shows one way a traditional craft can inspire clothing made for the present.","sourceReferences":["https://www.fdc.am/designers/5"],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"d2615e88-ffc5-5d42-aee3-a5fc7496d9db","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-25","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-25","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-DB-25","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The plain top helps keep the audience focused on the drawings during the presentation. The speaker still likes the other shirt.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The rehearsal showed that the shiny shirt distracted attention."},{"key":"b","text":"The speaker still likes it and plans to wear it later."},{"key":"c","text":"The party is where the speaker plans to wear the shiny shirt."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Main message of AUDIO-A","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-L01","ENG7-U01-L03","ENG7-U01-L05","ENG7-U01-L07"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-25","ENG7-U01-MA-25"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-MB-25","ENG7-U01-MC-25"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Integrate the rehearsal observation with the clothing change while preserving the later party plan. Familiar comfort preferences or the writing model do not supply the attention-related reason.","completeSolution":"The plain top helps keep the audience focused on the drawings during the presentation. The speaker still likes the other shirt.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-DB-AUDIO-A","kind":"listening","format":"script","familyId":"357e658b-ca9e-513b-aa1b-27cb65a74e15","title":"Listening source DB-A","locale":"en","text":"speaker: For my class presentation, I first chose a shirt with large shiny decorations. At rehearsal, my partner kept looking at the shirt instead of the drawings I was explaining. I wanted the drawings to get the attention, so I chose a plain dark top for the presentation. I still like the shiny shirt, and I will wear it at our club party afterwards. I put it in a separate cloth bag to keep the decorations from catching on my other clothes. Choosing the plain top was about this activity, not giving up my favourite style.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"283f8432-6fd2-543b-a636-14113dbfed07","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-26","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-DB-26","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-DB-26","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"All three suggestions help a new member understand and participate in the club.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The suggestions do not set clothing choices."},{"key":"b","text":"Each suggestion supports joining the club."},{"key":"c","text":"No lost materials are described."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_varian