ceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MB-25","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The speaker learns to allow time for a contribution instead of judging interest from initial silence.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"Daniel''s later notes and offer challenge the first assumption."},{"key":"b","text":"The account directly challenges that generalisation."},{"key":"c","text":"No such rule is proposed."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Main message of AUDIO-A","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-L01","ENG7-U01-L03","ENG7-U01-L05","ENG7-U01-L07"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-25","ENG7-U01-MA-25"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-25","ENG7-U01-MC-25"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Reconcile first impression with later evidence and identify a limited lesson, avoiding an opposite universal stereotype about all quiet people.","completeSolution":"The speaker learns to allow time for a contribution instead of judging interest from initial silence.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MB-AUDIO-A","kind":"listening","format":"script","familyId":"f374699d-be6c-5e9b-9392-bae2ff8b4775","title":"Listening source MB-A","locale":"en","text":"speaker: When our group met for the first time, Daniel said very little. I thought he did not want to help with our presentation. Later, he showed us a page of notes. He had written down all the jobs we needed to do and noticed that nobody had offered to prepare the introduction. He offered to do it. I realised he had been listening and thinking. Next time, I will give a quiet member time to share an idea before deciding that they are not interested.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"75a3c76a-0cc3-59f7-a542-b5c6afcb60e6","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MB-26","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MB-26","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MB-26","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The students plan ways to get useful responses before choosing details of the T-shirt design.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"All three suggestions improve how the group gets reactions."},{"key":"b","text":"No borrowed hats are involved."},{"key":"c","text":"No such competition is proposed."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Overall message of AUDIO-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-L01","ENG7-U01-L03","ENG7-U01-L05","ENG7-U01-L07"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-26","ENG7-U01-MA-26"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-26","ENG7-U01-MC-26"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Unify different feedback methods while distinguishing obtaining evidence from dictating the final design.","completeSolution":"The students plan ways to get useful responses before choosing details of the T-shirt design.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MB-AUDIO-B","kind":"listening","format":"script","familyId":"b70d3969-78c0-5551-bb5b-4fd5fc67c393","title":"Listening source MB-B","locale":"en","text":"narrator: Listen to three students discussing how to get feedback on a club T-shirt design. You will hear each speaker''s number.\n\nspeaker_1: Speaker One. Let''s give everyone a card. They can write one thing they like and one thing they would change, without writing their name.\n\nspeaker_2: Speaker Two. I want to show the design on a real T-shirt first. A small drawing may not show how the picture looks when someone wears it.\n\nspeaker_3: Speaker Three. We should ask a clear question about the lettering. Can people read the club name from across the room? That would help us choose its size.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"ce88a76b-67a9-5103-a7b8-ed59d1e9e73f","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MB-27","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MB-27","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MB-27","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"Daniel offers to prepare the introduction.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"No clothing-selection job is assigned to him."},{"key":"b","text":"The introduction is the job nobody had taken."},{"key":"c","text":"The recording does not mention this offer."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Relevant explicit detail from AUDIO-A","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-L02","ENG7-U01-L04","ENG7-U01-L06","ENG7-U01-L08","ENG7-U01-L09","ENG7-U01-L10"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-27","ENG7-U01-MA-27"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-27","ENG7-U01-MC-27"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Retrieve the exact missing role identified in Daniel''s notes; the gist about quiet participation does not reveal that role.","completeSolution":"Daniel offers to prepare the introduction.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MB-AUDIO-A","kind":"listening","format":"script","familyId":"f374699d-be6c-5e9b-9392-bae2ff8b4775","title":"Listening source MB-A","locale":"en","text":"speaker: When our group met for the first time, Daniel said very little. I thought he did not want to help with our presentation. Later, he showed us a page of notes. He had written down all the jobs we needed to do and noticed that nobody had offered to prepare the introduction. He offered to do it. I realised he had been listening and thinking. Next time, I will give a quiet member time to share an idea before deciding that they are not interested.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"e4a9c8d7-8a98-5165-a431-f0139ef0c81d","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MB-28","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MB-28","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MB-28","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"Speaker One proposes cards without the writer''s name.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"Speaker One proposes unsigned cards."},{"key":"b","text":"Speaker Two proposes showing the design on a real shirt."},{"key":"c","text":"Speaker Three proposes a question about readable lettering."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Attribute a stated view to a speaker in AUDIO-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-L02","ENG7-U01-L04","ENG7-U01-L06","ENG7-U01-L08","ENG7-U01-L09","ENG7-U01-L10"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-28","ENG7-U01-MA-28"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-28","ENG7-U01-MC-28"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Identify the anonymity condition tied to one method, rather than the physical display or lettering question supplied by the others.","