 seats.","rejectedExamples":["chairs enough","enough space"]},{"id":"f2","text":"Space answers the need for room to move; enough precedes the noun.","rejectedExamples":["space enough","enough chairs"]}],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Enough with adjectives and nouns","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-P16","ENG7-U01-P17","ENG7-U01-P18","ENG7-U01-P39"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-13","ENG7-U01-MA-13"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-13","ENG7-U01-MB-13"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Distinguish sufficient object count from insufficient usable space without treating one as evidence for the other. Both noun phrases require correct enough placement and contextual assignment.","completeSolution":"Enough chairs provides seats; not enough space limits movement. The two statements can both be true.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":null}},{"itemId":"7f9a2113-36e8-5d18-aa65-058bd8c7b13b","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-14","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-14","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 14; activities 15; programme T1.K3; docs/content/english-7-unit-