 remains unanswered.","optionFeedback":[],"fieldFeedback":[{"id":"f1","text":"Creativity is a general abstract mass noun in this sentence.","rejectedExamples":["a","an","the"]}],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Explicit zero article","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-P25","ENG7-U01-P26","ENG7-U01-P27","ENG7-U01-P41"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-20","ENG7-U01-MA-20"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-20","ENG7-U01-MB-20"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Apply general reference to an abstract quality rather than to physical materials or plural objects; no claim about one specific person''s quality is supplied.","completeSolution":"Write zero for creativity in general. The sentence does not identify a particular instance, and a blank remains unanswered.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":null}},{"itemId":"5c2ee852-5f61-5659-a0e3-f5c03207eae4","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-21","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-21","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 17, 18; activities 19; programme T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MC-21","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"Concrete colours, shapes and clothing parts help readers imagine the costumes without photographs.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The revision adds details and keeps opinions separate."},{"key":"b","text":"The colours, shapes and parts address the stated problem."},{"key":"c","text":"The guide does not ask for a beauty ranking."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Main idea of READ-A","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R02","ENG7-U01-R04","ENG7-U01-R05","ENG7-U01-R06","ENG7-U01-R09","ENG7-U01-P23","ENG7-U01-P24"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-21","ENG7-U01-MA-21"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-21","ENG7-U01-MB-21"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Link the audience''s information need to the change in writing; avoid treating any added adjective or stronger opinion as a sufficient description.","completeSolution":"Concrete colours, shapes and clothing parts help readers imagine the costumes without photographs.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MC-READ-A","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"a0f73378-c629-58d1-a194-2e6f443cb43f","title":"Reading source MC-A","locale":"en","text":"A class prepared a guide to costumes for visitors who would not see the display. The first draft said only that each costume was beautiful or unusual. When a classmate read it without the photographs, those words did not help her imagine the clothes.\n\nThe writers added colours, shapes and parts such as collars and sleeves. They kept opinions in a separate final sentence. For one jacket, they described a short green body with long yellow sleeves. The revised guide gave readers concrete information before offering an opinion.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"beea1d76-3417-5a78-a57c-e1f6df748369","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-22","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-22","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 17, 18; activities 19; programme T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MC-22","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The jacket has a short green body and long yellow sleeves.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"This reverses the supplied colour and length details."},{"key":"b","text":"This preserves both parts of the description."},{"key":"c","text":"The sleeves are long and yellow, not short and green."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Supported explicit detail from READ-A","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R02","ENG7-U01-R04","ENG7-U01-R05","ENG7-U01-R06","ENG7-U01-R09","ENG7-U01-P23","ENG7-U01-P24"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-22","ENG7-U01-MA-22"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-22","ENG7-U01-MB-22"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Bind colour and length to two garment parts; the plausible distractors exchange or repeat features instead of adding unrelated information.","completeSolution":"The jacket has a short green body and long yellow sleeves.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MC-READ-A","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"a0f73378-c629-58d1-a194-2e6f443cb43f","title":"Reading source MC-A","locale":"en","text":"A class prepared a guide to costumes for visitors who would not see the display. The first draft said only that each costume was beautiful or unusual. When a classmate read it without the photographs, those words did not help her imagine the clothes.\n\nThe writers added colours, shapes and parts such as collars and sleeves. They kept opinions in a separate final sentence. For one jacket, they described a short green body with long yellow sleeves. The revised guide gave readers concrete information before offering an opinion.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"2f4b61d0-d3ac-5dd4-a7ec-e5b1c6afb159","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-23","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-23","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 16, 20, 21; activities 18, 21, 22; programme T1.K2, T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MC-23","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The passage links preserving older clothing with modern use of traditional elements while keeping the activities distinct.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"This preserves both activities and their relationship."},{"key":"b","text":"The passage distinguishes recreation from modern use of elements."},{"key":"c","text":"Recreating traditional clothing is explicitly included."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Chronology or contrast from READ-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R01","ENG7-U01-R03","ENG7-U01-R07","ENG7-U01-R08"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-23","ENG7-U01-MA-23"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-23","ENG7-U01-MB-23"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Interpret a contrast between two cultural-design practices; unlike the four other profile chronology items, no unsupported order is imposed on simultaneous activities.","completeSolution":"The passage links preserving older clothing with modern use of traditional elements while keeping the activities distinct.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MC-READ-B","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"a864e540-7a9e-533f-9bca-06febf414330","title":"Reading source MC-B","locale":"en","text":"The Fashion and Design Chamber of Armenia describes two connected activities at the Teryan Cultural Center. One is carefully recreating traditional Armenian clothing with advice from experts who study culture and traditions. Another is making modern clothes and accessories that use traditional elements.\n\nThe center also offers opportunities to learn traditional crafts. In this account, preserving older designs and using cultural ideas in present-day work are connected, but they are not described as exactly the same activity.","sourceReferences":["https://www.fdc.am/designers/45"],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"72afd1f2-8f45-5e64-a1fe-d0e7ec69870a","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-24","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-24","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 16, 20, 21; activities 18, 21, 22; programme T1.K2, T1.L2; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MC-24","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The passage names experts who study culture and traditions.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"No colour vote is described."},{"key":"b","text":"Expert advice is explicitly named."},{"key":"c","text":"The passage does not assign this role only to sellers."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Supported cultural information from READ-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-R01","ENG7-U01-R03","ENG7-U01-R07","ENG7-U01-R08"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-24","ENG7-U01-MA-24"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-24","ENG7-U01-MB-24"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Locate the stated source of historical-cultural advice, rather than infer expertise from sales or visitor preference.","completeSolution":"The passage names experts who study culture and traditions.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MC-READ-B","kind":"reading","format":"passage","familyId":"a864e540-7a9e-533f-9bca-06febf414330","title":"Reading source MC-B","locale":"en","text":"The Fashion and Design Chamber of Armenia describes two connected activities at the Teryan Cultural Center. One is carefully recreating traditional Armenian clothing with advice from experts who study culture and traditions. Another is making modern clothes and accessories that use traditional elements.\n\nThe center also offers opportunities to learn traditional crafts. In this account, preserving older designs and using cultural ideas in present-day work are connected, but they are not described as exactly the same activity.","sourceReferences":["https://www.fdc.am/designers/45"],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"ca51e7a3-267e-5673-a8b8-888759fa051f","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-25","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-25","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MC-25","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"The revised survey makes the occasion clear, helping the speaker interpret different clothing choices.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The revised questions preserve differences."},{"key":"b","text":"Naming occasions makes the choices easier to interpret."},{"key":"c","text":"A space for explanation is added for the walk."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Main message of AUDIO-A","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-L01","ENG7-U01-L03","ENG7-U01-L05","ENG7-U01-L07"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-25","ENG7-U01-MA-25"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-25","ENG7-U01-MB-25"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Infer the purpose of replacing one general preference question with occasion-specific questions; do not mistake clearer categories for a demand for uniform preferences.","completeSolution":"The revised survey makes the occasion clear, helping the speaker interpret different clothing choices.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MC-AUDIO-A","kind":"listening","format":"script","familyId":"5e6facc4-e703-5701-9379-33f109ef6761","title":"Listening source MC-A","locale":"en","text":"speaker: For our class survey, I first asked, ''Which clothes do you like best?'' Several classmates said that it depended on what they were doing. So I changed the survey. I asked about a walk, a family celebration and a day at home separately. The answers were easier to understand because each question named an occasion. For the walk, I also left a space for people to explain their choice. Many wrote about being able to move comfortably. I learned that one general question had hidden useful differences.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"b6d3e488-d2e2-5372-a1df-a768d79f8e78","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-26","context":{"schemaVersion":"haiedu-authoring-review-v1","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-26","version":1,"locale":"en","sourcePacket":"docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json","sourceReference":"Grigoryan, English 7, Zangak 2023; pp. 6, 144; activities 8; programme T1.L1; docs/content/english-7-unit-01-assessment-batch-bcd.json#ENG7-U01-MC-26","hint":"Use the supplied information and preserve its meaning.","feedback":"All three students suggest ways to make progress despite different design preferences.","optionFeedback":[{"key":"a","text":"The suggestions do not demand one colour."},{"key":"b","text":"Each proposes a way to make progress on the disagreement."},{"key":"c","text":"None proposes cancelling the play."}],"fieldFeedback":[],"comparison":{"disposition":"protected_parallel_assessment_variant","protocol":"haiedu-protected-parallel-pilot-v1","authorization":"docs/evidence/english-7-unit-01-owner-acceptance-20261021.json","repeatedTaughtClaim":"Overall message of AUDIO-B","nearestPractice":["ENG7-U01-L01","ENG7-U01-L03","ENG7-U01-L05","ENG7-U01-L07"],"nearestExistingAssessment":["ENG7-U01-DA-26","ENG7-U01-MA-26"],"nearestBatch":["ENG7-U01-DB-26","ENG7-U01-MB-26"],"newStimulusInterpretation":"Infer the common constructive purpose across a test, a shared goal and a staged decision process; the specific solutions remain distinct.","completeSolution":"All three students suggest ways to make progress despite different design preferences.","guideRelationship":"The existing Unit 1 guide teaches this procedure. Its worked examples do not give this complete contextual answer. The procedure remains familiar; no independent new reasoning coverage is claimed.","protectionJudgment":"Reserve this exact stimulus and its derivatives to this form. Fresh interpretation is an automated-author judgment; human content, SME and exposure qualification remain pending. Do not show its source or solution in Practice or Chapter Review.","independentNewReasoningClaimed":false,"semanticReviewer":"Codex automated author; independent human review pending"},"source":{"id":"ENG7-U01-MC-AUDIO-B","kind":"listening","format":"script","familyId":"3ca844ae-c14e-5420-ae24-3e0519a0316d","title":"Listening source MC-B","locale":"en","text":"narrator: Listen to three students suggesting ways to settle a disagreement about a costume for a school play. You will hear each speaker''s number.\n\nspeaker_1: Speaker One. We could try both ideas in a short rehearsal. Then we would know which one lets the actor move more easily, instead of only guessing.\n\nspeaker_2: Speaker Two. Let''s remember what the character needs to do in the scene. We all want the audience to understand the character, even though we prefer different designs.\n\nspeaker_3: Speaker Three. Perhaps we can decide on the shape first and discuss the colours afterwards. Trying to settle every detail at once is making the discussion harder.","sourceReferences":[],"reviewStatus":"pending","registrationStatus":"unregistered","audioAvailable":false}}},{"itemId":"9cfaf9c8-e50a-5e10-afec-bde42c18b2ba","itemCode":"ENG7-U01-MC-27","context":{"schemaVersion":"haie